      },
      "message": "fix(post): Sodick wire skims on their own LN condition words\n\nThe Sodick wire post refused every skimmed Wire Contour, so no 2- or\n3-pass LN1W / LN2W job could post. Sodick's 2012 LN1W / LN2W training\nmanual shows the next pass's C word after the return to the start point,\nwith the wire left threaded. The post now writes each skim's C word\nthere (one T91, one T90), refuses a skim condition id that is not a C\nword by name, and offers the opt-in option approachCondition that cuts\nthe first approach move on C000. With the option off, the existing\ngoldens do not change.\n\nFixes #2649\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
